  2. Full Self-Improvement Loop

  What: Wire the nightly review's tomorrow_suggestions into the morning briefing ("I noticed you often ask about X on Mondays —
  should I pre-fetch that?"), and let Jarvis propose user preference updates (update_user_profile) directly from the nightly review
  instead of waiting for a conversation. Add a self_score metric (response quality 1-5, rated by the LLM itself post-analysis)
  tracked in Redis — reflection cycles use it to detect degradation trends.
  Why it matters: Currently Jarvis learns facts passively from conversations. This makes learning active and proactive — it notices
  patterns and acts on them between sessions.
  Entry point: self.py nightly review → add proposed_profile_updates field; briefing.py → inject tomorrow_suggestions; analyzer.py →
   add self_score field.

  3. JarvisApp Push Notifications

  What: Add APNs (Apple Push Notification service) delivery to main.py. Store device tokens in Redis (apns:token:{user_code}),
  registered at app launch via a new POST /apns/register endpoint. Trade alerts, briefing delivery, and self-reflection
  send_notification actions all get an APNs path alongside (or replacing) the Gmail path. Notifications deep-link into the relevant
  conversation session.
  Why it matters: Currently Jarvis can only push to Gmail. Push notifications make trading alerts and proactive suggestions
  actionable in seconds instead of minutes, and eliminate the Gmail round-trip.
  Entry point: main.py new /apns/register endpoint; trading.py push_pending_alert + APNs call; self.py _action_send_notification +
  APNs fallback; JarvisAPI.swift device token registration on launch.
